------------------------------------------------------------
-- Requests to other modules
------------------------------------------------------------
-- REQUEST accounts/User.prohibit_login, accounts/User.is_active, accounts/User.is_admin: used by transport (fixed names).
-- REQUEST accounts/owner_visibility_is_public(repository): owner (user or org) visibility = public, for anonymous fetch.
-- REQUEST authentication/has_two_factor(user), must_have_two_factor(user), authenticated_by_password(user): password HTTP git is always refused (decided: tokens only); enforced-2FA blocks SSH.
-- REQUEST keys/SshKey.grants_read_on(repository) / grants_write_on(repository): deploy key modes (used directly and inside may_write_code / may_write_branch).
-- REQUEST keys/new_commits_verified(repository, old_sha, new_sha): every new commit has a verified signature (require_signed_commits).
-- REQUEST keys/can_sign_as(user, repository, branch): instance signing policy for CRUD actions (needed when the branch requires signed commits).
-- REQUEST organizations/member_of_any_team(user, teams) (is the user in any of these teams), organizations/can_create_org_repo(user, org).
-- REQUEST repositories/Repository.is_template, is_private, is_fork, is_empty, is_mirror, is_archived, status, default_branch: written by post-receive (is_empty, default_branch, is_private, is_template).
-- REQUEST repositories: react to PushToCreateRequested (create repo), PushReceived (size, updated time), CommitsPushed (auto-watch pusher).
-- REQUEST pulls/PullRequest.allow_maintainer_edit and maintainer_edit_allows(user, repository, branch_name): maintainers pushing to a PR head branch.
-- REQUEST pulls/PullRequest.may_merge(user) (exists) and pulls/merge_requirements_met(pull) (approvals, status checks, rejected reviews, outdated branch, protected files): used by AcceptProtectedBranchMergePush.
-- REQUEST pulls/pull_by_index, is_agit_pull, pull_poster, open_agit_pull, agit_pull_for (refs/pull/<n>/head): AGit flow lookups.
-- REQUEST pulls: react to AgitPullRequestRequested, AgitPullRequestHeadPushed, MergePushCompleted, BranchDeleted, BranchRenamed, CommitsPushed, BranchProtectionChanged, CommitStatusCreated.
-- REQUEST releases/release_exists(repository, tag_name), releases/has_published_release(repository, tag_name); react to TagCreated/TagUpdated/TagDeleted for tag-only releases.
-- REQUEST quota/exceeds_git_quota(repository), quota/exceeds_lfs_quota(repository): owner over size quota for git / LFS.
-- REQUEST issues: react to CommitsPushed for close/reopen keywords and commit references.
-- REQUEST actions: react to DefaultBranchChanged / BranchRenamed (cancel schedules). Job results arrive as actions/JobCommitStatusReported (done).
-- REQUEST keys: keys_of_repository(keys, repository) = the given DeployKeys attached to repository (allowlist filtering, decided code 4/5).
-- REQUEST notifications: a deploy-key push (code/PushReceived with push.pusher = null, push.deploy_key set) is shown in the feed as by the deploy key (its name), never the repository owner (decided code 4); BranchCreated/BranchDeleted then carry by = null.
-- REQUEST actions / webhooks / issues / repositories / discovery / pulls / releases: code/Push.pusher, CommitsPushed.pusher, RefCreated/RefDeleted.pusher, BranchCreated/BranchDeleted.by and TagCreated/TagUpdated/TagDeleted.by are null for a deploy-key push; use push.deploy_key (doer/sender = the key; no auto-watch; no issue references attributed to a user) (decided code 4).
